text:
maria: heads up — after the runtime patch deployed last night we're seeing a spike in requests that call external tools where the adapter returns malformed JSON and our pipeline is treating that as a fatal schema rejection. Users see 500s instead of a graceful fallback. :eyes:

jamal: ugh. do we have an example payload?

maria: yep, saved one from logs: ```{"tool": "search", "output": "{\"title\": "X", "link\": "http://..."}"}``` the inner string was double-encoded by the adapter so our validator tries to parse to object and fails with a TypeError.

sasha: that exact case should be nonfatal — we should accept string-encoded blobs and route to a text fallback. Wasn't that the fallback behavior pre-patch? :thinking_face:

jamal: right. pre-patch behavior: if tool output doesn't match shape => mark event.warn and send original text through model as last-resort. Post-patch we changed the deserialization order and now validation happens earlier and triggers a hard reject.

kevin: I pushed the patch to deserializers to improve speed; didn't expect the validation ordering to change. Sorry, my mistake. Quick mitigation: short rollback or change validator to try-catch parse errors and convert string->json when possible.

maria: mitigation plan suggestion: 1) add try/catch around tool-adapter parse, 2) if parse fails but field is string, treat as raw_text and set response.flags: nonfatal_tool_schema 3) increment telemetry counter tool_schema.soft_accept so we can measure impact.

ops-bot: Incident created: INC-2026-134, severity=low, assigned=eng-platform.ack

jamal: also need to think about routing — these failures are concentrated on East-1 GPU pool because adapter version there is older. Could add a temporary routing rule to prefer east-2 or fallback to model variant that doesn't require tool calls. That avoids user-visible failures while we patch adapters.

sasha: agree. We should add a console toggle (rollout switch) to flip strict_schema=true/false per-route. Product wants strict by default but we need a per-customer/canary knob.

kevin: I'll open a PR with the try/catch + telemetry. Quick patch: ```js
// pseudocode
try {
  let parsed = JSON.parse(toolResp.output);
  validateShape(parsed);
} catch (e) {
  if (typeof toolResp.output === 'string') {
    metrics.increment('tool_schema.soft_accept');
    response = { raw_text: toolResp.output, nonfatal: true };
  } else {
    throw e; // keep current hard reject
  }
}
```

maria: can we gate that behind a feature flag so we can canary to 10%? We don't want silent acceptance hiding real contract regressions.

kevin: yes — will use rollout flag: runtime.features.tool_soft_accept with percentage and route-level override. Will also emit a new dimension in logs: adapter_version so we can correlate.

jamal: for dashboards: add a per-model and per-route chart for tool_schema.soft_accept vs tool_schema.hard_reject and an alert if hard_reject spikes > 0.5% over baseline. Also include adapter_version heatmap.

ops-bot: Deploy pipeline note: will schedule hotfix on canary pool at 05:00 UTC, then expand to 10% traffic.

sasha: assignable tasks: @kevin patch + FF (ETA 3h), @maria add dashboard + alert (ETA 4h), @jamal routing rule to prefer east-2 (ETA 1h).

maria: thanks. let's also add a short note in the release channel explaining the user-visible 500s and the plan so support has talking points. :white_check_mark:

kevin: on it. I'll include sample log queries and the PR link.

jamal: after patch, follow-up: we should add a policy doc about strict vs soft validation and how it interacts with quotas and retries — currently soft_accept bypass still counts against tool call quota, is that ok?

maria: good call — for soft_accept we should consider not charging quota or track separately. Add to backlog if not urgent.

sasha: ok closing loop here. will update INC with runbook and mark for review in retro. :thumbsup:
